Multi-threaded PLE n-gram gather, 2-pass SMEM-compacted QSA select, and granular profile markers

1. Parallelizes host PLE n-gram gather (`Gather.main` in `cuda_batch_state.zig`) across
   8 CPU threads for prompt chunks >= 512 rows, cutting `ple` GPU stall from 155.7 ms ->
   16.6 ms on 16K prefill and 35.2 ms -> 9.3 ms on 245K prefill (100% bit-exact).
2. Upgrades `fn_qsa_select_body` (`flashnext_batch.cu`) to 2-global-pass SMEM-compacted
   radix select (11-bit top pass + compact <=4096 candidates into 40 KiB SMEM + SMEM
   passes 1-2 + exact tie-breaking + 512-element bitonic sort), cutting 245K `qsa_select`
   from 69.4 ms -> 51.0 ms and 248K cold prefill from 128.45s -> 125.85s (1,966.4 tok/s).
3. Adds granular `attn_sub` (prep/pool/score/select/core/gate) and `exp_prompt`
   (routed4/shared6) timing lines under `TF_FLASHNEXT_PROFILE=1`.

